WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.621
Prepare Cluster A under a generic datacenter group in Global Config.

00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:09.301
Keep separate references for each required purpose and preserve the exact existing

00:00:09.301 --> 00:00:12.234
keys. Save grouping stores labels only.

00:00:12.368 --> 00:00:16.072
Save to ZTF stores changed credential and provider settings.

00:00:16.208 --> 00:00:20.409
Labels do not change permissions, targets or selected vault behavior.

00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:25.202
In Config Files, organize reviewed YAML by datacenter, cluster

00:00:25.381 --> 00:00:30.014
and purpose. Existing files can remain Ungrouped until you assign them.

00:00:30.171 --> 00:00:32.254
Selecting a group narrows the library;

00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:34.003
it does not rewrite the YAML.

00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:38.554
Open the intended file and confirm its actual cluster and credential references.

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:43.231
Open YAML Studio. Select the datacenter and cluster context,

00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:45.578
or choose a deliberate manual target.

00:00:45.799 --> 00:00:50.463
Choose a task, complete its guided fields, and review the generated YAML.

00:00:50.578 --> 00:00:53.178
Advanced YAML remains available when needed.

00:00:53.405 --> 00:00:54.856
The context helps authoring;

00:00:54.856 --> 00:00:57.337
it does not grant execution permission.

00:00:57.672 --> 00:00:59.690
Select Validate configuration.

00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:03.901
Review syntax, workflow shape and declared credential references

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:07.653
separately. A declared reference does not prove authentication.

00:01:07.795 --> 00:01:11.805
Live preflight remains Not run until its execution-specific check is

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:16.328
performed. Changing the draft invalidates earlier validation, so validate

00:01:16.328 --> 00:01:20.544
again before saving. Give the file a descriptive name and use Validate

00:01:20.595 --> 00:01:24.695
and save. Select an existing pipeline, review the proposed action

00:01:24.916 --> 00:01:27.724
and saved file, then confirm the handoff.

00:01:27.946 --> 00:01:31.565
It appends one reviewed step while keeping existing steps in order.

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.424
Open Pipelines for approval and execution;

00:01:34.603 --> 00:01:37.112
saving and handoff start no job.
